A system is dependent when

- some row is zero: $512-7^3=169$ systems;
- otherwise, two rows are equal: $7^3-7\cdot6\cdot5=133$ systems;
- otherwise, the three distinct nonzero rows are dependent. Two distinct nonzero $0/1$ vectors are never parallel, so one row is in the span of the other two; by the table above, the triple is $\{u,v,u+v\}$ with $u,v$ of disjoint support. There is one such triple per disjoint pair, so $6$ triples (e.g. $\{100,010,110\}$, $\{100,011,111\}$), giving $6\cdot3!=36$ ordered systems.

Total: $169+133+36=338$.

**Answer: (B) 338**
